_hint() {
  cat <<'MSG'
==> xps15-display-color: factory ICC installed to
      /usr/share/color/icc/xps15-display-color/xps15-9530-lgd06b3-factory.icc

    colord scans that directory and auto-attaches the profile to the internal panel
    by EDID md5 (03f8beceddb5ad49941b8d45e90c45a3). No manual binding needed.

    Verify (as your normal user, not root):
      colormgr get-devices | grep -A6 '0x06b3'          # profile listed on the panel
      colormgr get-profiles | grep -B4 xps15-display    # DATA_source=calib present

    If a stale per-user copy exists it will shadow this one — remove it and let the
    packaged profile take over:
      rm -f ~/.local/share/icc/Dell-XPS15-9530-LGD06B3-factory.icc
      systemctl --user restart xdg-desktop-portal 2>/dev/null; sudo systemctl restart colord

    Note: the profile carries no vcgt, so the desktop's appearance does not change.
    It is consumed by colour-managed apps only (GIMP, Krita, darktable, Inkscape,
    Firefox with gfx.color_management.mode=1). See:
      /usr/share/doc/xps15-display-color/README

    Rollback:
      sudo pacman -R xps15-display-color
MSG
}

post_install() { _hint; }

post_upgrade() { _hint; }

post_remove() {
  cat <<'MSG'
==> xps15-display-color removed. colord falls back to the EDID-derived profile
    that mutter generates automatically. Restart colord to drop it immediately:
      sudo systemctl restart colord
MSG
}
